Wed Oct  7 09:06:21 UTC 2026 - Fridrich Strba <fstrba@suse.com>

- Update to version 6.13.0
  * New Features
    + Add support for permitted subclasses
    + Add RecordComponentInfo.getAttribute(byte tag)
    + Add Const.MAJOR_27
    + Add Const.MINOR_27
    + Add and use ArrayType.isElementType(Type)
    + Add Const.MAJOR_28
    + Add Const.MINOR_28
  * Fixed Bugs
    + Fix constant pool module access test on Java 26 and above
    + Deprecate org.apache.bcel.classfile.Utility.Utility()
    + Deprecate org.apache.bcel.verifier.exc.Utility
      .getStackTrace(Throwable)
    + Fix all Javadoc warnings and enforce checks by default
    + Escape constant pool names in generated HTML
    + Escape referenced names in BCELFactory Java output
    + Make wide flag thread-local in Utility.codeToString
    + Read multianewarray dimensions as unsigned byte
    + Site docs: clarify security model
    + Read ConstantDynamic indices as unsigned shorts
    + Validate index upper bound in CPInstruction, IINC and RET
      setIndex
    + Use correct attribute tag in NestHost and ModuleMainClass
    + Propagate runtime-visible flag when parsing parameter
      annotations
    + Use fixedLength for parsed LOOKUPSWITCH length
    + Fix ConstantPoolGen dedup key collisions for names with
      delimiters
    + Read unsigned bytecode operands in CodeHTML disassembler
    + Deep-copy bootstrap arguments array in BootstrapMethod.copy()
    + Use exclusive live-range end in LocalVariableTable
      .getLocalVariable
    + Build TABLESWITCH from sorted arrays in SWITCH
    + Use array element type not basic type for primitive array
      access
    + Set length in INVOKEDYNAMIC constructor
    + Reject CALOAD on non-char arrays in structural verification
    + Add negative verifier tests for remaining array load/store
      component type checks
    + Validate u1 count bound in INVOKEINTERFACE and MULTIANEWARRAY
    + Match wide local variable instruction length to dumped bytes
    + Bound IINC increment to signed short
    + Fix SpotBugs USO_UNSAFE_METHOD_SYNCHRONIZATION in ConstantUtf8
    + Nested Code/Record attributes drive unbounded parse-time
      recursion in ClassParser
    + Nested annotation element values recurse unboundedly;
      MAX_ARRAY_DIMENSIONS cap bypassed
    + Opcodes tableswitch and lookupswitch add boundary checks
    + JustIce Pass 2 hangs on cyclic superclass chain of a
      referenced exception class
    + JustIce Pass 2 LVT check amplifies each 10-byte entry into
      ~131k hashtable operations
    + Pass 3b dataflow stores frames per instruction and clones
      ever-growing execution chains
    + Cubic handlers × range × subroutines scan in Subroutines
      constructor hangs JustIce Pass 3b
    + Subroutines.noRecursiveCalls enumerates exponentially many JSR
      call paths
    + Disassembler and Class2HTML re-implement the unchecked
      switch-table allocation
    + ConstantPool.constantToString recurses forever on
      self-referencing CONSTANT_MethodHandle
    + Utility.typeSignatureToString recurses per generic-nesting
      level, unbounded, with quadratic substring copies
    + Repositories cache classes under the input-defined this_class
      name; global static Repository/VerifierFactory make the
      poisoning ClassLoader-wide (bsc#1284400, CVE-2026-94114)
    + Silent u2/u1 count truncation across dump paths corrupts
      emitted bytecode
    + Class2HTML emitters write attacker class-file strings into
      HTML unescaped (stored XSS in reports) (bsc#1284399,
      CVE-2026-105111)
    + Class2HTML builds output file paths from the unvalidated class
      name
    + ClassPath.getBytes() sizes its buffer from the forged ZIP
      uncompressed-size field
    + PMG attribute ignores declared length, enabling BCEL-vs-JVM
      parse divergence
    + Signature.matchGJIdent recurses unboundedly on nested generic
      signatures (Signature.translate)
    + Utility.decode fixed 3x buffer breaks the encode/decode round
      trip and throws unchecked AIOOBE
    + BCELifier interpolates attacker class/package names into
      generated Java source unescaped
    + Verifier pass 3a delayed checks are quadratic in attribute and
      code size
    + Verifier cache grows unboundedly with attacker-chosen class
      names
    + Static WIDE ThreadLocal survives exceptions, corrupting the
      next class's disassembly on the same thread
    + Utility.JavaReader escape decoding: OOB table index, bad-hex
      crash, silent non-canonical aliasing
  * Changes
    + Bump org.apache.commons:commons-parent from 95 to 104
    + Bump org.jetbrains.kotlin:kotlin-stdlib from 2.3.0 to 2.4.20
    + Bump commons-io:commons-io from 2.21.0 to 2.22.0
    + Bump jna.version from 5.18.1 to 5.19.1
    + [test] Bump org.apache.commons:commons-collections4 from 4.5.0
      to 4.6.0
- Changes of version 6.12.0
  * New Features
    + Add Const.MAJOR_26
    + Add Const.MINOR_26
  * Fixed Bugs
    + Fix infinite loop in example.TransitiveHull
    + Fix Apache RAT plugin console warnings
    + Fix malformed Javadoc comments
    + Make the build reproducible on the Azul JDK
    + Fix infinite loop in JavaClass.findField() on invalid input
    + Fix infinite loop in JavaClass.getAllInterfaces() on invalid
      input
    + Fix infinite loop in JavaClass.getSuperClasses() on invalid
      input
    + Exception message in Args.requireU4() refers to the wrong data
      type
    + Exception message in Args.requireU2() refers to the wrong
      upper range value
    + Code.Code(int, int, DataInput, ConstantPool) now throws a
      ClassFormatException if the code array is greater than the
      JVM specification allows
    + Code.Code(int, int, int, int, byte[], CodeException[],
      Attribute[], ConstantPool) now throws a ClassFormatException
      if the code array is greater than the JVM specification allows
    + Code.setCode(byte[]) now throws a ClassFormatException if the
      code array is greater than the JVM specification allows
    + ClassDumper.dump() should not call the input stream it didn't
      open; fixes IOException when calling DumpClass.main
      (ClassDumper.java:351)
    + org.apache.bcel.classfile.ConstantPool.ConstantPool(Constant[])
      now uses varagrs: ConstantPool(Constant...)
    + org.apache.bcel.classfile.Deprecated now requires its the
      attribute_length item be zero
    + org.apache.bcel.classfile.Synthetic now requires its the
      attribute_length item be zero
    + The size of an Attribute unknown to the JVM specification is
      limited to 1 MB and is overridden with the system property
      BCEL.Attribute.Unknown.max_attribute_length
  * Changes
    + Bump org.apache.commons:commons-parent from 89 to 95
    + [test] Bump org.jetbrains.kotlin:kotlin-stdlib from 2.2.20 to
      2.3.0
    + Bump commons-io:commons-io from 2.20.0 to 2.21.0
    + Bump commons-lang3 from 3.19.0 to 3.20.0
    + [test] Bump org.apache.commons:commons-exec from 1.5.0 to
      1.6.0
- Changes of version 6.11.0
  * New Features
    + Add Const.MAJOR_25
    + Add Const.MINOR_25
    + Add experimental CycloneDX VEX file
    + Refactor to use new Maven POM variable ecj.version
  * Fixed Bugs
    + Replace internal use of Locale.ENGLISH with Locale.ROOT
    + BCEL-375: Wrong permissions on bcel .jar file in binary
      .tar.gz distribution file
    + BCEL-376: ClassPath.close() throws
      UnsupportedOperationException when created with
      system-classpath
    + ClassPath.getResources(String) can use an ArrayList instead of
      a Vector
    + Fix SpotBugs [ERROR] Medium: Operation on the "created" shared
      variable in "ConstantUtf8" class is not atomic [org.apache
      .bcel.classfile.ConstantUtf8] At ConstantUtf8.java:[line 119]
      AT_NONATOMIC_OPERATIONS_ON_SHARED_VARIABLE
    + Fix SpotBugs [ERROR] Medium: Operation on the "considered"
      shared variable in "ConstantUtf8" class is not atomic [org
      .apache.bcel.classfile.ConstantUtf8] At ConstantUtf8.java:
      [line 137] AT_NONATOMIC_OPERATIONS_ON_SHARED_VARIABLE
    + Fix SpotBugs [ERROR] Medium: Operation on the "skipped" shared
      variable in "ConstantUtf8" class is not atomic [org.apache
      .bcel.classfile.ConstantUtf8] At ConstantUtf8.java:[line 134]
      AT_NONATOMIC_OPERATIONS_ON_SHARED_VARIABLE
    + org.apache.bcel.util.ClassPath
      .addJdkModules(String, List<String>) now reads the system
